<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Poltava</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1709</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Poltava · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Poltava was fought in 1709 in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, where the army of Peter I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> decisively defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a>. The Swedish army was destroyed and its remnants capitulated soon afterwards. The battle marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> as a great power and the emergence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> as the dominant force in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava.jpg" alt="Battle of Poltava" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre-Denis Martin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marten%27s_Poltava.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
